      "problem": "Isabella took $2$ hours to wash $12$ windows. If she washes the windows at a steady pace, then what statement describes the unit rate?",
      "worked_solution": "The ratio of washed windows to hours is $12:2.$ So we start with the ratio $12:2$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12}{2}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $1$ by dividing the numerator and denominator by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12÷2}{2÷2}=\\frac{6}{1}\n$$\n\nConsequently, Isabella washed $6$ windows per hour.",
